---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import AwsArchitecture from '../components/AwsArchitecture.astro';
import markPortrait from '../../images/MarkPro.webp';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero-home">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">AWS solutions architecture / federal technology leadership</p>
      <h1><em>I connect the AWS architecture to the mission it serves.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-aside" data-reveal>
      <p>I work across cloud services, security boundaries, data flows, and operations—and lead the people and decisions that turn an architecture into a working system. My federal program experience keeps technical choices tied to users, funding, and delivery.</p>
      <p class="capability-line">AWS architecture · Applied AI · Federal mission systems · Program leadership</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="#aws-architecture">Explore my AWS approach <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/markgingrass/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hire me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-portrait">
      <Image src={markPortrait} alt="Mark Gingrass in his home office" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 160px, 260px" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-rail" aria-label="Career at a glance">
    <div class="proof-grid">
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>37</strong><span>Weapon systems</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>12,000</strong><span>Engines</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>$6.3B+</strong><span>Annual budget authority</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>15M+</strong><span>Records integrated in CIRDS</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>400+</strong><span>Regulatory scientists served</span></div>
      <div class="proof-item"><strong>GS-14</strong><span>Program leadership / COR III · 20+ years in federal technology</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="proof-note">The weapon systems, engines, and budget figures are from my previous role as a logistics supply chain manager for 448 SCMW.</p>
  </section>

  <AwsArchitecture />

  <section class="section fda-lead" aria-labelledby="fda-title">
    <div class="shell case-grid">
      <div class="case-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Leading AI in government / FDA</p>
        <h2 id="fda-title">Paving the way for AI in FDA research tracking.</h2>
        <p class="lead-statement">I’m leading FDA’s first research tracking system integrated with AI. Program management, team leadership, stakeholder alignment, and technical direction sit together in my role.</p>
        <p>At the Center for Tobacco Products, I’m moving that work forward inside the agency boundary. The AI checks research abstracts against the governing coding manual, returns supporting evidence, and flags disagreements. FDA reviewers make the final call.</p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/work/#applied-ai">My role. The decisions. The work. <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-steps">
        <div class="case-step"><span>01</span><div><h3>Lead the program.</h3><p>Set priorities, coordinate teams and vendors, and keep delivery tied to the mission.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>02</span><div><h3>Manage the stakeholders.</h3><p>Bring scientific, business, and technical needs into the same decision. Work through disagreements and keep people moving.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Shape the architecture.</h3><p>Fit AI into the existing research workflow and agency boundary. Require evidence. Keep decision authority with reviewers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>04</span><div><h3>Connect funding to delivery.</h3><p>Connect investment and acquisition decisions to scope, ownership, and work the teams can execute.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section project-proof" aria-labelledby="tutorialrepo-title">
    <div class="shell project-proof-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="project-label">Architecture in practice / TutorialRepo</p>
        <h2 id="tutorialrepo-title">A working product is one proof point.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>I direct the architecture for TutorialRepo across AWS delivery, AI, a publishing pipeline, and a native iOS client. The platform is designed to support more courses on the same foundation. I carry the decisions through release and ongoing operation.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/work/#tutorialrepo">See the architecture decisions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading
        label="Lean / management / investment"
        title="Before funding the solution, question the work."
        body="Before making it faster, ask whether it needs to happen at all. I use Lean thinking to simplify, change, or stop work before committing technology, people, and funding. Then I connect mission priorities to architecture, acquisition, and delivery."
      />
      <div class="role-grid">
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Set the direction.</h3>
          <p>I set the direction, prioritize through both an enterprise and product owner lens, get the right people involved, and work with the team all the way through implementation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Challenge the architecture.</h3>
          <p>I look past the technical solution itself, challenge the assumptions behind it, and connect the decisions back to the mission and business need.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Own delivery.</h3>
          <p>I establish clear ownership, address problems early, and keep teams and vendors focused on building something that actually works for the people using it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="role-card" data-reveal>
          <h3>Lead teams and vendors.</h3>
          <p>I’ve led complex vendor environments for years, from onboarding new teams to coordinating multiple vendors, subcontractors, and projects running at the same time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="identity-panel">
    <div class="identity-copy">
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label">The through-line</p>
        <blockquote>Solve the real problem.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Air Force veteran. Former Program Manager in the DoD’s U.S. Air Force Supply Chain Management Wing, working in logistics and Art of the Possible. Electrical engineering and computer science background. MBA. GS-14 program manager and COR III. I’ve spent more than 20 years in federal technology. I know how programs get stuck, how vendors drift, and how good technical decisions get lost. I expect technology investments to produce something useful and justify what they cost. I also know how to get the work moving again.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/profile/">More about how I operate <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact writing-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeading index="02" label="Field notes" title="Writing about systems, incentives, and the decisions between them." />
      <div class="writing-grid">
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Federal IT</span><h3>The certificate warning nobody reads</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">Applied AI</span><h3>The AI solution trap</h3><p>Read on Substack ↗</p>
        </a>
        <a class="writing-card" href="https://newsletter.markgingrass.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-reveal>
          <span class="micro-label">All dispatches</span><h3>Notes from the intersection of public mission and modern technology.</h3><p>Browse the newsletter ↗</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
